mploys approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $216K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["MasterBrand, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.4B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -3.4pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $118M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.33\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.4pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 103% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0320691829564903},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 81/100): structural revenue/margin decline; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (36% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 60% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MasterBrand (MBC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/masterbrand-mbc-q3-2026-earnings-164942000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793984471.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.19,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MasterBrand Inc (MBC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: Net Loss Amid American Woodmark ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/masterbrand-inc-mbc-q3-2026-072136446.html","date":"2026-11-06",